course: dictionary
lesson: 14923
title: Refrigeration
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Refrigeration means keeping things cold, especially food and medicine, using a fridge, a freezer or another cooling machine.
explain: Look at the clues in this sentence: «The milk stays fresh for longer because of refrigeration.» Fresh milk and a cold machine are the clues, so refrigeration must be the cold that stops food going bad.
explain: The word can also mean the machines and technology that make things cold. When you meet it, ask: what would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Refrigeration means keeping things cold, using a fridge, freezer or other cooling machine.
fact: Refrigeration slows down the growth of bacteria, so food stays fresh for longer.
fact: Fridges should be below about 5 °C (41 °F) to keep food safe.
fact: Before refrigeration, people used ice houses, salt and smoking to keep food.
fact: Some labels say «keep refrigerated» or «requires refrigeration after opening».
exercise: «Before refrigeration, people salted and smoked fish to stop it going bad.» What is refrigeration? | *Keeping things cold with a fridge or freezer | Cooking food in a hot oven | Growing vegetables in a garden | Selling food in a shop
exercise: «The label says: keep refrigerated after opening.» What does this tell you to do? | Throw it away at once | Keep it in the sun | Shake it well | *Keep it cold
exercise: Ella says refrigeration is a kind of cooking with heat. Is she right? | Yes, it means cooking food with heat | *No, it means keeping things cold | No, it means eating food quickly | Yes, it means baking bread
test: «The milk stays fresh for longer because of refrigeration.» Why does refrigeration help food last longer? | Cold makes food grow bigger | Cold makes food hotter | Cold changes food into water | *Cold slows down the growth of bacteria
test: What temperature should a fridge be below to keep food safe? | About 15 °C | About 50 °C | *About 5 °C | About 25 °C
exam: Which of these uses refrigeration to keep food cold? | A pair of socks | A wooden spoon | A paper map | *A fridge
